    Both rows were dispatched by the 2026-11-17 17:45 wave, whose workers died
    after doing the work but before committing/closing (BTL-COMPARE-1's tree was
    fully staged; RELEASE-010's two CHANGELOG commits were on its branch). The
    wave manifest had no finished_at and no worker process was alive.
    
    This tick recovered both: BTL-COMPARE-1's staged tree was committed verbatim
    (5a4a67f), RELEASE-010's commits were verified against its own acceptance
    criteria (bac9823), both were merged serially into main and pushed
    (origin/main a8cb167).
    
    Gates on the merged tree: full CI-mirroring suite 4776 passed / 8 skipped /
    4 deselected, ruff clean, mypy clean, scripts/release_check.py rc=0, GitHub
    Actions green on a8cb167.
    
    Tier 2 verdicts: BTL-COMPARE-1 bf4abdeb PASS (tier1+2), RELEASE-010 babfd93f
    PASS (tier1+2, all criteria).
    
    Also repaired this repo's venv console script: venv/bin/gitreins was a stale
    editable install of 0.10.2 whose source path no longer exists
    (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'gitreins.cli'), which aborted every
    `git commit` in this checkout before the message was even read. Reinstalled
    gitreins 0.21.0 (pipx-matching version) into the venv; `gitreins --version`
    now reports 0.21.0.
    
