d from the reasoning's ACCEPTANCE paragraph into executable form (field was null); dispatchable next tick. Doc seam deferred to a follow-up row.", "acceptance_criteria": "1) src/observability/metrics.py declares and exposes: aipp_emulator_desync_total (counter), aipp_emulator_frame_stale_seconds (gauge), aipp_screenshot_bytes (gauge), aipp_runlog_bytes (gauge), aipp_runlog_last_write_timestamp_seconds (gauge), aipp_bridge_requests_total{cmd,outcome} (counter), aipp_bridge_active_connections (gauge) - all registered on the existing REGISTRY and served by GET /metrics/prometheus. Proof: a test asserting each family name+labels appears in a collected sample, plus a curl of /metrics/prometheus showing the seven families. 2) The desync signal is introduced as a DOCUMENTED PROXY in the module docstring (repeated identical frame hash combined with an unchanged RAM tile) and the code must not claim a true RAM-vs-frame comparator (no such comparator exists; spec 8.6). Proof: docstring quoted in the report + a test that feeds the same frame hash twice and asserts the counter increments once. 3) scripts/game_bridge.py emits aipp_bridge_requests_total{cmd,outcome} on EVERY request path, including the currently-swallowed reply-error path (except Exception: pass around :441-444), and tracks aipp_bridge_active_connections so it returns to 0 when connections close. Proof: a test that forces a raising reply path and asserts outcome=error increments, and a burst test asserting the gauge returns to 0. 4) Data-growth gauges are computed from the real locations (screenshots/run_<id>/ and cron_logs/) at a documented measurement point, with a test on a tmp fixture. 5) Acceptance evidence: the PromQL shapes from the row text (time() - aipp_runlog_last_write_timestamp_seconds > 3600; min/max of the gauges) are exercised in-process via prometheus_client and the desync counter is shown incrementing on a deliberately corrupted boot-state fixture with before/after values pasted. 6) docs/observa