-{"complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T19:25:03.973526Z", "id": "QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-28", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "QA tick ai-plays-poke-qa-2026-11-04-18-51-39, server bunker-mvp, agent 52b86a36. Sequence: 'bunker-qa.sh launch' returned LAUNCHED and wrote .meta phase=launched; the battery finished (~16 min) and the agent-side marker ~/qa-run.finished existed; 'bunker-qa.sh collect --evidence <same path>' then printed only 'COLLECT-ADOPT reason=recent tick-death-orphan agent=52b86a36 new_tick_pid=348951' after syncing 24 rows and qa-evidence.jsonl.logs/qa-logs-3428505, and exited WITHOUT destroying the agent \u2014 the agent was still listed by 'bunker list --server bunker-mvp --status all' afterwards and had to be destroyed by hand. A detached launch's controller pid is always dead by collect time, so this branch is not an edge case: it fires on the normal launch\u2192collect lifecycle. Consequence 1: capacity leak \u2014 /tmp/bunker-qa-orphans held 9 locks when this tick launched (174b3780, 4e9fec9b, ccc4a5f8, ceb9ebc3, cf73b3aa, db92ed44, e8d3215a, f04fb4bd, f58144a5) and bunker-las-03 was still running agents ccc4a5f8 (4.5 GB) and cf-node. Consequence 2: this tick's launch spent 19:51Z->19:03Z (about 12 minutes) inside qa_cleanup_orphan_agents before spawning anything, because each loop iteration calls 'bunker destroy' with no per-destroy timeout (f04fb4bd alone ran 4m22s and then reported 'orphan remains destroy_rc=1'); a failed destroy keeps its lock, so every later launch pays the same cost again. Consequence 3: the reaper's evidence quarantine fails with 'QUARANTINE-FAIL ... mkdir -p /var/lib/bunker-qa/quarantine/<agent>-<ts> rc=1' for every agent on a remote server (it tries to mkdir on the host running the controller), so orphan evidence is never preserved. This is harness-class, not an ai-plays-poke product defect; it is filed here because this lane hit it and it invalidates battery throughput fleet-wide. Evidence: /home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratc