 {"id":"VISION-GRID-UNIFY","title":"[P1] one grid, one legend: unify the 9x9 vision-grid definition with the reader 10x9 (R-001)","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":"2","depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"The project invariant says one grid, one symbol set, one legend for both channels. Measured contradiction: src/core/vision_grid.py declares GRID_COLS=9, GRID_ROWS=9, PLAYER_CELL=(4,4) while src/core/ram_reader.py renders render_tile_grid(cols=10, rows=9) and the live console places the facing arrow at row 3, col 4. The vertical result is the measured one-row offset (RAM walls rows 0-1, vision rows 1-2) and every cell-by-cell verdict is shifted by construction. Fix: one shared module (or constants imported from one place) defining cols, rows, cell pixels, origin and player cell; both consumers import it. Spec refs: R-001 in specs/contracts/_matrix.md, FLOW-01 in specs/flows/. Do not tune prompts or models to compensate - the geometry is the defect.","acceptance":"1) vision_grid.py and ram_reader.py resolve grid geometry from ONE module (grep shows a single definition of GRID_COLS/GRID_ROWS/PLAYER_CELL in src/). 2) The console serves ram and vision rows of equal length (9x10) with the arrow at the same cell in both. 3) A test asserts the two renderers agree on player cell for a fixture state. 4) The verdict agree/conflict counts change by more than the offset alone (sanctioned: numbers may shift when the defect is fixed).","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/ai_plays_poke-VISION-GRID-UNIFY","branch":"wt/VISION-GRID-UNIFY","commit_hash":"ac9945f9388c58252596e9ee429c03250414ecfd","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","foreman_note":"Merged as a9116da. gitreins: tier1 PASS, tier2 PASS (history run aa9c1cf9, verdict a4287790). First complete attempt was killed by a foreground tool timeout leaving NO verdict while the task still showed complete; the retry on a c