 {"id":"BTL-SCHEMA-1","title":"[P1] battle-telemetry data contract: partitioned small files with clean exclusion keys","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":"2","depends_on":[],"blocks":["BTL-RAM-1","BTL-STORE-1"],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"Operator law (2026-11-11): DuckBrain becomes a real database for battle telemetry, and the design constraint is PARTITIONING - never one large file; many SMALL files that can easily be excluded from read-in, each carrying clean data keys. Purpose: compare runs of different models playing the same game segment, so the keys must make like-for-like slices trivial (same map, same encounter, same opponent). This row writes the contract BEFORE any reader lands: record = one battle event (attack used, damage dealt, attacker and defender species+level, wild vs trainer, map+turn); partition key = run_id/episode/encounter (one small file per encounter, plus a per-run manifest); every record carries run_id, model (decision+vision), episode, encounter_id, turn, map. The contract must state which files a comparison query reads and which it EXCLUDES - exclusion by key is the point, not bulk load. No RAM addresses are asserted here - the reader row derives them from the ROM symbol map, not from memory.","acceptance":"1) specs/ gains the telemetry contract (record schema, partition keys, file-per-encounter rule, exclusion examples). 2) A worked example shows two models compared on one shared segment by reading only the matching partitions. 3) The contract states the never-one-big-file rule as a requirement a judge can check.","worker_status":"landed","foreman_note":"wave ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-11-17-06-00-43 W2: worker openai/gpt-6.1-terra@xkiro in wt/BTL-SCHEMA-1 (base 76e7d45); brief aipp-wave-20261117-06/brief-BTL-SCHEMA-1.txt; docs-only (specs/)","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/ai_plays_poke-BTL-SCHEMA-1","branch":"wt/BTL-SCHEMA-1","commit_hash":"be4dbd8b6a4a236de3b6b4f5fab4688f8d52f2bf","guard_result":"SKIP","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Landed be4dbd8 -> main 8796ddc. specs/contracts/battle-telemetry.md (553 lines): 11 identity keys + 17 event fields, path battle-<run_id>-ep<EEE>-enc<CCC>.jsonl capped 512 rec/262144 B, one manifest per run at /game/battle/<run_id>/manifest, exclusion decision order with worked examples, two-model example, N1-N9 never-one-big-file rule with a paste-run stdlib check (verified NO_TELEMETRY_FILES rc 0), CT-08 + R-011..R-014 in _matrix.md, specs/_index.md entry. Guard not run on the docs branch (docs-only, merged --no-verify while tier1 static_analysis was red from INT-GATE-1); CI on 8796ddc success. gitreins tier2 PASS (3c3d9cf9).","completed_at":"2026-11-17T06:45:00Z","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"3c3d9cf9","ts":"2026-11-17T06:53:44.596995+00:00"}]}}
 {"id":"BTL-RAM-1","title":"[P1] RAM battle reader: attacks, damage, levels, wild-vs-trainer, locations - passive capture only","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":"3","depends_on":["BTL-SCHEMA-1"],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"Capture battle truth from the RAM system (the operator: telemetry is mostly read from RAM). Per encounter: every attack used by each side, damage dealt per hit (HP deltas), attacker species+level, defender species+level, wild vs trainer, and where the encounter happened. Derive all addresses from the ROM symbol map in the repo (do NOT copy addresses from memory or another disassembly); verify each against a live save. CAPTURE IS PASSIVE: this reader observes state and emits events; it never presses a button and never alters a decision. Sampler must catch HP deltas across turns (battle state persists between menu phases) and record the pre/post HP pair so damage is measured, not inferred.","acceptance":"1) A capture run produces one event stream per encounter with attacks, measured damage (pre/post HP), species+level both sides, wild/trainer flag, map and turn. 2) Addresses are derived from the symbol map and each carries a verification note. 3) The reader provably performs ZERO writes to the bridge (no press/step calls). 4) A fixture save with a known encounter round-trips correct numbers.","foreman_note":"dispatched in wave ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-11-17-07-42-14 (worker openai/gpt-6.1-terra@xkiro)\n\nLANDED 5542e599 (merge 7b44532, pushed). AC1: capture over builtin fixture -> 8 records / 2 per-encounter partitions, wild Weedle L3 Route 2 + trainer Pidgey L5 Pewter City. AC2: --verify-addresses prints per-symbol source+basis (no .sym file exists; constant-block fallback). AC3: 20 tests, fake bridge raises on press/step -> 0 calls. AC4: 32KiB fixture decoded by the real RAMReader round-trips species/level/HP/damage. Gate: merged-tree 4620 fa