 {"id":"BTL-STORE-1","title":"[P1] DuckBrain store: append-only partitioned writes for battle telemetry","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":"2","depends_on":["BTL-SCHEMA-1","BTL-RAM-1"],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"Implement the store per the contract: DuckBrain as the raw database, one SMALL file per encounter partition, clean keys on every record (run_id, model, episode, encounter_id, turn, map), append-only - never rewrite a partition. A per-run manifest indexes the partitions so a comparison query reads exactly the matching encounters and excludes the rest BY KEY. Writes must be idempotent per encounter (a re-run of the same partition replaces its manifest entry, not duplicates it). This treats DuckBrain as a real database: raw data lands first; interpretation happens in the comparison layer, never at write time.","acceptance":"1) N encounters produce N small files plus one manifest - proven, not asserted, by listing the partitions after a capture. 2) A comparison for one model+segment reads only the keyed partitions (the exclusion is visible in what the query opens). 3) Re-writing the same encounter is idempotent (no duplicate partitions). 4) No record is mutated after append.","foreman_note":"dispatched in wave ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-11-17-10-10-24 (worker openai/gpt-6.1-terra@xkiro, base c27ab5a). ACs restated from the prose row into executable form (row acceptance was null): store module writes contract-shaped partitions per specs/contracts/battle-telemetry.md 4/5/7/9, 512-record/262144-byte caps with continued_from, idempotent per-encounter write, manifest at /game/battle/<run_id>/manifest with E1..E6 keys; proofs = tests/test_battle_store.py green + scripts/store_battle_telemetry.py --verify.\n\nLANDED a913552 (merge 1467a4c, pushed). 3 new files, 2365 lines: src/core/battle_telemetry_store.py, scripts/store_battle_telemetry.py, tests/test_battle_store.py. Contract conformance per specs/contracts/battle-telemetry.md 4/5/7/9: partition path battle-<run_id>-ep<EEE>-enc<CCC>.jsonl under namespace pokemon-battle, 512-record/262144-byte caps with continued_from continuation, idempotent per-encounter append (manifest entry replaced, records skipped by identity hash), one manifest per run at /game/battle/<run_id>/manifest with all E1..E6 index keys, code-level N1/N8/N9 refusals, R1..R6 enforcement with dropped_records. FOREMAN VERIFY: pytest tests/test_battle_store.py -> 40 passed in 0.66s; ruff check on all 3 files clean; store CLI --verify rc=0 (vacuous, no telemetry files on this host); worker pre-commit full suite 4703 passed 27 skipped. WORKER-DISCLOSED LIMITS: dropped_records counts the ingesting process only (partitions do not record refused inputs); 512-record cap exercised with synthetic records; run-loop wiring (cron_runner.py) untouched by design. VERDICT PENDING.\n\nCLOSED on pass2 verdict 12763360: TIER1 PASS (lint+secrets+tests) and 3 of 4 tier2 criteria PASS with live end-to-end evidence (500-record CLI write -> two partitions 261673B/256 recs and 249612B/244 recs, continued_from chain, md5sum -c OK on re-run, written=0 skipped=500, single memories line, --verify PASS/PASS, 40 tests green). The 4th criterion FAILed on a JUDGE REPRO ERROR, disproved by the foreman: the judge claimed R4's zero-damage branch is unreachable and 'reproduced' it with defender_hp_before=15, defender_hp_after=15, damage=0 - a self-consistent record R4 permits. Foreman repro (scratch/r4_check2.py using the repo's own make_record): miss damage=0 before=15 after=10 -> REFUSED 'R4: damage 0 != defender_hp_before-defender_hp_after (15-10=5)'; damage 15->10 with damage=3 -> REFUSED R4. R4 is enforced via the arithmetic branch (src/core/battle_telemetry_store.py:440-453). First verdict 65492b80 had tier2 PASS and failed tier1 only on the pre-fix 'ruff check .' scope (fixed in f3afab3). CI GREEN on merge 1467a4c.","worktree":"/home/kara/